From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:24:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: h616: use the 256-bit DDR mode

With the DDR mode in VE_MODE set to 128-bit, which the driver uses on
all SoCs, the H616 reads corrupted reference chroma, while luma is
fine. H.264, VP8 and VC-1 inter pictures come out with bit-exact luma,
but with wrong chroma, which builds up from picture to picture.

The vendor library selects the DDR mode based on the VE IC version. It
uses the 256-bit mode without the 2 MiB reconstruction write mode on
the H616, and keeps the 128-bit mode with the 2 MiB reconstruction
write mode on older SoCs, like the H6. Doing the same on the H616 makes
all codecs bit-exact.

Make the VE_MODE DDR settings a variant property and use the 256-bit
mode on the H616. Replace the FIXME about the DDR mode with a
description of what the vendor library does.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c    |  2 ++
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h    |  2 ++
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 3 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
index b0f002f8aa86..3d2ef4b7893a 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include "cedrus_video.h"
 #include "cedrus_dec.h"
 #include "cedrus_hw.h"
+#include "cedrus_regs.h"
 
 static int cedrus_try_ctrl(struct v4l2_ctrl *ctrl)
 {
@@ -815,6 +816,7 @@ static const struct cedrus_variant sun50i_h616_cedrus_variant = {
 			  CEDRUS_CAPABILITY_VP9_DEC |
 			  CEDRUS_CAPABILITY_VC1_DEC,
 	.mod_rate	= 600000000,
+	.ve_mode_ddr	= VE_MODE_DDR_MODE_BW_256,
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id cedrus_dt_match[] = {
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h
index 0f3b0f811e62..139229bf7f68 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h
@@ -218,6 +218,7 @@ struct cedrus_dec_ops {
 struct cedrus_variant {
 	unsigned int	capabilities;
 	unsigned int	mod_rate;
+	u32		ve_mode_ddr;
 };
 
 struct cedrus_dev {
@@ -241,6 +242,7 @@ struct cedrus_dev {
 	struct reset_control	*rstc;
 
 	unsigned int		capabilities;
+	u32			ve_mode_ddr;
 
 	struct delayed_work	watchdog_work;
 };
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
index 45dd036c132f..adf8be36f7c7 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
@@ -36,11 +36,16 @@ int cedrus_engine_enable(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx)
 	u32 reg = 0;
 
 	/*
-	 * FIXME: This is only valid on 32-bits DDR's, we should test
-	 * it on the A13/A33.
+	 * The DDR mode depends on the SoC. Like the vendor library, use the
+	 * 128-bit mode with the 2 MiB reconstruction write mode, unless the
+	 * variant says otherwise.
 	 */
-	reg |= VE_MODE_REC_WR_MODE_2MB;
-	reg |= VE_MODE_DDR_MODE_BW_128;
+	if (ctx->dev->ve_mode_ddr) {
+		reg |= ctx->dev->ve_mode_ddr;
+	} else {
+		reg |= VE_MODE_REC_WR_MODE_2MB;
+		reg |= VE_MODE_DDR_MODE_BW_128;
+	}
 
 	switch (ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat) {
 	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG2_SLICE:
@@ -320,6 +325,7 @@ int cedrus_hw_probe(struct cedrus_dev *dev)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	dev->capabilities = variant->capabilities;
+	dev->ve_mode_ddr = variant->ve_mode_ddr;
 
 	irq_dec = platform_get_irq(dev->pdev, 0);
 	if (irq_dec <= 0)
